# Line endings, pinned.
#
# This repository is built around byte-identical artifacts. §31.4 asks every edition to reproduce
# the conformance corpus byte for byte, `tools/check-mirrors.mjs` asserts that a shared document is
# the same file in both repositories, and `versionDigest()` hashes source bytes into a package's
# identity. All three of those are decided by the exact contents of a file, and on a machine with
# `core.autocrlf=true` a checkout rewrites every line ending on the way in.
#
# So the working tree is LF everywhere, on every platform. Without this, the mirror check reports
# two identical documents as diverged — which it did, permanently, until this file existed, and a
# check that is always red is a check nobody reads.
#
# Existing files keep whatever endings they were committed with until they are renormalised:
#
#     git add --renormalize .
#
# which is a whitespace-only change and is best made on its own.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Anything whose bytes are its meaning is never touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.so binary
*.a binary
*.stl binary
*.dae binary
